# Cloudflare Pages headers. Read from the build output, so this file lives in
# public/ and Astro copies it into dist/.
#
# IMPORTANT: Pages APPENDS the headers of every matching rule rather than
# letting a more specific rule override a broader one. So a Cache-Control in a
# /* rule lands on the hashed assets too, and the resulting header is a
# concatenation like "max-age=31536000, immutable, max-age=0, must-revalidate".
# That is why /* below carries security headers only, and caching is set solely
# on the paths that should be cached. Fonts live under /_astro/ already, so
# they need no rule of their own.

# Content-hashed by the build: a new build means a new URL, so cache forever.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Everything, HTML included. No Cache-Control here on purpose — Pages already
# revalidates HTML by default, which is what a site the client edits herself
# several times a year wants.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
